Add a driver for the Transmeta Code Morphing Software ROM update service
(MSR 0x80868000-0x80868005): fw_upload for the CMS, recovery CMS, OEM
configuration table, boot code and write cycle components, and sysfs
read-back of the ROM components.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

diff -urNp a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-transmeta-cms b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-transmeta-cms
--- a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-transmeta-cms	1970-01-01 01:00:00.000000000 +0100
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-transmeta-cms	2026-11-11 08:09:09.034050865 +0100
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+What:		/sys/devices/faux/transmeta_cms/rom/<component>
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
+Description:
+		(RO, root only) Contents of a boot ROM component of a Transmeta
+		Crusoe or Efficeon processor, read through the Code Morphing
+		Software (CMS) ROM update service (MSR 0x80868000-0x80868005).
+		<component> is one of cms, recovery-cms, oem-config, boot-code
+		and write-cycle; only components CMS reports are present. The
+		ROM is read again whenever the file is read from offset 0.
+
+What:		/sys/class/firmware/tmta-<component>/
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
+Description:
+		Firmware upload interface (see sysfs-class-firmware) for each
+		present ROM component: tmta-cms, tmta-recovery-cms,
+		tmta-oem-config, tmta-boot-code and tmta-write-cycle. The image
+		is a signed CMS upgrade envelope (.cru); CMS checks the
+		envelope, vendor, processor and compatibility fields and the
+		DSA signature before it programs the ROM. CMS error codes are
+		logged with the SoftPatch error text.
